{
 "what": "DEV vs OFFICIAL plant case records (RUN_PLAN_amend_2 §8.2: any difference from the DEV record is reported)",
 "spec": "RUN_PLAN_amend_2.md v2.1 (FROZEN acdb1290...) §8.2 :533-537",
 "rule": "Records are matched on (plant, cell, case) - the case number the driver records (spec.case_of; P24 / P25: the map case; P3b: 1000 + i), unique within a cell (asserted on both sides). Every recorded field is compared except the per-process ones (VOLATILE: wall / CPU seconds, start / finish times, worker pid, peak working set and the memory flag derived from it): every per-case decision (booleans, statuses), every p and every other number, and the recorded seed keys (the `seeds` records: construction and leg entropies, integer site seeds). A record is flattened to leaf paths (dict keys joined by '/', list items by index; a list of scalars is one leaf); values are compared exactly (JSON equality; NaN equals NaN), and a numeric difference carries |dev - official| and whether it is within 1e-12 relative (REL_TOL: floating-point noise, e.g. a share computed through BLAS in another process; reported like every other difference, and counted apart from the material ones). Each difference is reported with its plant, cell, case, i, field path, category (seed key / decision / p / number / other), the DEV value, the official value and the DEV pass it came from; a field present on one side only is a difference (value \"<absent>\"). A DEV record with no official record of the same (plant, cell, case) is listed as DEV-only (not a difference: the official cases file holds the cases the official run used), and a plant whose official cases file is missing is flagged. The DEV passes are also compared among themselves on the cases they share (they must agree: same keys, same code).",
